[[:db/retract 17592186338641 :answer-field/choices 17592186337200] [:db/retract 17592186338641 :answer-field/choices 17592186337489] [:db/retract 17592186338641 :answer-field/choices 17592186336034] [:db/retract 17592186338641 :answer-field/choices 17592186337829] [:db/retract 17592186338641 :answer-field/choices 17592186338117] [:db/retract 17592186375329 :answer-field/choices 17592186375330] [:db/retract 17592186375329 :answer-field/choices 17592186375331] [:db/retract 17592186375329 :answer-field/choices 17592186375332] [:db/retract 17592186375329 :answer-field/choices 17592186375333] [:db/retract 17592186375329 :answer-field/choices 17592186375334] [:db/retract 17592186373175 :answer-field/choices 17592186373176] [:db/retract 17592186373175 :answer-field/choices 17592186373177] [:db/retract 17592186373175 :answer-field/choices 17592186373178] [:db/retract 17592186373175 :answer-field/choices 17592186373179] [:db/retract 17592186373175 :answer-field/choices 17592186373180] [:db/retract 17592186129841 :question/answer-fields 17592186128527] {:db/id 17592186129167 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-df61b368-91ad-5f51-9082-c280e6c8c895"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129168 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-ed99a179-e753-5cd2-8fc5-79553f622379"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186128988 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the parabola $y=x^2$ and the line $y=4?$\n\nI. It is a type I region\n\nII. It is a type II region\n\nIII. It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "question-df61b368-91ad-5f51-9082-c280e6c8c895" :question/id #uuid "df61b368-91ad-5f51-9082-c280e6c8c895" :question/math-academy-id "q-72139" :question/problem "![](images/2c/2cd94016388c0c128c6b2997fc9c04563f73b7024436b219f4adccc42640a331.png)\n\nWhich of the following represents the shaded region above as a type I region in two-dimensional space?" :question/worked-solution "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type I region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $x:$\n\n$$\nx=(2-y)^{3}\\,⟹\\,y=2-\\sqrt[3]{x}\n$$\n\nThe function $y=\\sqrt{x}+2$ is already written as a function of $x.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the vertical lines $x=0$ and $x=1.$ So, we have $0\\le x\\le 1.$\n\nWe draw a vertical arrow through the region to determine the lower function $g(x)$ and the upper function $f(x).$ A vertical line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type I region.\n\n![](images/95/95c5a0ddac341f0787fa020df5e04096287262ddc85441a93712bdaeee94eb0a.png)\n\nThe vertical line enters the region through the lower function $y=2-\\sqrt[3]{x}$ and leaves through the upper function $y=\\sqrt{x}+2.$ So, we have $2-\\sqrt[3]{x}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}+2.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,2-\\sqrt[3]{x}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}+2\\}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-02213c19-3d37-5f6e-a878-095eaddb24cd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-02213c19-3d37-5f6e-a878-095eaddb24cd" :answer-field/id #uuid "02213c19-3d37-5f6e-a878-095eaddb24cd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-ab02480e-b5bb-5f35-a6f4-5757d9e99b56" :answer-field/choices ["answer-b9405813-fc17-5099-a829-e0ea29c59df3" "answer-3a5bd8aa-e2c6-5754-937f-9b6671d7c03f" "answer-25d88735-5257-5296-9c68-7e1d6906875f" "answer-ab02480e-b5bb-5f35-a6f4-5757d9e99b56" "answer-f8dd14c9-648d-540a-b1b9-2d8d593af4cb"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b9405813-fc17-5099-a829-e0ea29c59df3" :answer/id #uuid "b9405813-fc17-5099-a829-e0ea29c59df3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le (y-2)^{2}\\le x(2-y)^{3},\\,0\\le y\\le 1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-3a5bd8aa-e2c6-5754-937f-9b6671d7c03f" :answer/id #uuid "3a5bd8aa-e2c6-5754-937f-9b6671d7c03f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le (2-y)^{3},\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}+2\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25d88735-5257-5296-9c68-7e1d6906875f" :answer/id #uuid "25d88735-5257-5296-9c68-7e1d6906875f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}+2\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ab02480e-b5bb-5f35-a6f4-5757d9e99b56" :answer/id #uuid "ab02480e-b5bb-5f35-a6f4-5757d9e99b56" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,2-\\sqrt[3]{x}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}+2\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f8dd14c9-648d-540a-b1b9-2d8d593af4cb" :answer/id #uuid "f8dd14c9-648d-540a-b1b9-2d8d593af4cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\sqrt[3]{x}+2\\le y\\le \\sqrt{x}+2\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129838 :question/worked-solution "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type I region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $x:$\n\n$$\nx=\\sqrt{y-3}\\,⟹\\,y={x}^{2}+3\n$$\n\nThe function $y=1$ is already written as a function of $x.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the vertical lines $x=0$ and $x=1.$ So, we have $0\\le x\\le 1.$\n\nWe draw a vertical arrow through the region to determine the lower function $g(x)$ and the upper function $f(x).$ A vertical line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type I region.\n\n![](images/43/43b35101f6c57352975f3667ca76dece5782326c9af008990c8820a71bed504d.png)\n\nThe vertical line enters the region through the lower function $y=1$ and leaves through the upper function $y={x}^{2}+3.$ So, we have $1\\le y\\le {x}^{2}+3.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le {x}^{2}+3\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186338641 :answer-field/correct "answer-ddf32d4b-35c9-53c9-8b7a-da0fab2ce17c" :answer-field/choices ["answer-ddf32d4b-35c9-53c9-8b7a-da0fab2ce17c" "answer-f35ff991-7f88-5bd4-ad43-0dc80f45077b" "answer-b72d10c6-5fff-5baf-9e3d-bf7492e4e118" "answer-96be98fa-6123-5adc-80a6-525122a1c1b7" "answer-db8db5e8-a2ba-5df6-8c21-465d5cc40018"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ddf32d4b-35c9-53c9-8b7a-da0fab2ce17c" :answer/id #uuid "ddf32d4b-35c9-53c9-8b7a-da0fab2ce17c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le {x}^{2}+3\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f35ff991-7f88-5bd4-ad43-0dc80f45077b" :answer/id #uuid "f35ff991-7f88-5bd4-ad43-0dc80f45077b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le {x}^{2}-3\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-b72d10c6-5fff-5baf-9e3d-bf7492e4e118" :answer/id #uuid "b72d10c6-5fff-5baf-9e3d-bf7492e4e118" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,1\\le y\\le {x}^{3}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-96be98fa-6123-5adc-80a6-525122a1c1b7" :answer/id #uuid "96be98fa-6123-5adc-80a6-525122a1c1b7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y-3},\\,1\\le y\\le 3\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-db8db5e8-a2ba-5df6-8c21-465d5cc40018" :answer/id #uuid "db8db5e8-a2ba-5df6-8c21-465d5cc40018" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y-3},\\,1\\le y\\le 4\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129837 :question/worked-solution "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type I region has the property that a vertical line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type I region is the following.\n\n![](images/d7/d74059ee4370e106b54917ec43b007327805049033752867473d08da850001bf.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186375314 :question/worked-solution "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type I region has the property that a vertical line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type I region is the following.\n\n![](images/bf/bf2098a7fcdecce8405dadf6f9cd2c78da19d1c0a7ae2c9c9e95a897a64ef9d9.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186375328 :question/worked-solution "A type I region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le x\\le b,\\,g(x)\\le y\\le f(x)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type I region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $x:$\n\n$$\nx=y+1\\,⟹\\,y=x-1\n$$\n\nThe function $y=\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}$ is already written as a function of $x.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the vertical lines $x=1$ and $x=3.$ So, we have $1\\le x\\le 3.$\n\nWe draw a vertical arrow through the region to determine the lower function $g(x)$ and the upper function $f(x).$ A vertical line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type I region.\n\n![](images/15/15f9c5d526747b80766a8a3250fa2e705d5d7d9561c52e08492b7a18f1483eb6.png)\n\nThe vertical line enters the region through the lower function $y=\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}$ and leaves through the upper function $y=x-1.$ So, we have $\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}\\le y\\le x-1.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}\\le y\\le x-1\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186375329 :answer-field/correct "answer-81fc323d-3d67-5381-ac5a-a4eff2e18c3e" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e7932458-6442-57f7-8677-554bfa971f00" "answer-a059210a-4218-5284-a342-d373e1d7610a" "answer-14ceafca-0ef0-5d60-bc6c-15fd2f018b65" "answer-81fc323d-3d67-5381-ac5a-a4eff2e18c3e" "answer-6f70b707-beb3-5c61-9042-eb57a0ba9c35"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e7932458-6442-57f7-8677-554bfa971f00" :answer/id #uuid "e7932458-6442-57f7-8677-554bfa971f00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}+1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a059210a-4218-5284-a342-d373e1d7610a" :answer/id #uuid "a059210a-4218-5284-a342-d373e1d7610a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le x\\le y+1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-14ceafca-0ef0-5d60-bc6c-15fd2f018b65" :answer/id #uuid "14ceafca-0ef0-5d60-bc6c-15fd2f018b65" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}\\le y\\le x+1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-81fc323d-3d67-5381-ac5a-a4eff2e18c3e" :answer/id #uuid "81fc323d-3d67-5381-ac5a-a4eff2e18c3e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 3,\\,\\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}\\le y\\le x-1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6f70b707-beb3-5c61-9042-eb57a0ba9c35" :answer/id #uuid "6f70b707-beb3-5c61-9042-eb57a0ba9c35" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le y+1,\\,0\\le y\\le \\frac{1}{2}(x-1)^{2}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-ed99a179-e753-5cd2-8fc5-79553f622379" :question/id #uuid "ed99a179-e753-5cd2-8fc5-79553f622379" :question/math-academy-id "q-168840" :question/problem "![](images/99/99c16d2b48da841b9ba6f3bc400701b26af36c8780d27293ddb68d433c27da3c.png)\n\nWhich of the following represents the shaded region above as a type II region in two-dimensional space?" :question/worked-solution "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type II region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $y:$\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x)+1\\,⟹\\,x={e}^{y-1}\n$$\n\nThe function $x=0$ is already written as a function of $y.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the horizontal lines $y=1$ and $y=2.$ So, we have $1\\le y\\le 2.$\n\nWe draw a horizontal arrow through the region to determine the left function $g(y)$ and the right function $f(y).$ A horizontal line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type II region.\n\n![](images/4f/4f9c46e1fa6cc373896c2905aab4c1ceca6ff4de7cd498297d4a02e5c4375a39.png)\n\nThe horizontal line enters the region through the lower function $x=0$ and leaves through the upper function $x={e}^{y-1}.$ So, we have $0\\le x\\le {e}^{y-1}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le x\\le {e}^{y-1}\\}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7d28adc9-c677-55f6-b557-2b7e9fd45782"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7d28adc9-c677-55f6-b557-2b7e9fd45782" :answer-field/id #uuid "7d28adc9-c677-55f6-b557-2b7e9fd45782" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-1c956e41-28d5-5cb3-80b8-79cc5871e46a" :answer-field/choices ["answer-794a009c-f53b-5f55-963d-5ca344d4e683" "answer-6575688f-64bd-5a5c-b00c-b61181f473fc" "answer-1c956e41-28d5-5cb3-80b8-79cc5871e46a" "answer-cd49c0c2-a640-5ea0-b993-a477ec76ed96" "answer-8ddecd47-8b29-538f-bf12-0e82ccc9537c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-794a009c-f53b-5f55-963d-5ca344d4e683" :answer/id #uuid "794a009c-f53b-5f55-963d-5ca344d4e683" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡y+1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-6575688f-64bd-5a5c-b00c-b61181f473fc" :answer/id #uuid "6575688f-64bd-5a5c-b00c-b61181f473fc" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le x\\le {e}^{y+1}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1c956e41-28d5-5cb3-80b8-79cc5871e46a" :answer/id #uuid "1c956e41-28d5-5cb3-80b8-79cc5871e46a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le 2,\\,0\\le x\\le {e}^{y-1}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cd49c0c2-a640-5ea0-b993-a477ec76ed96" :answer/id #uuid "cd49c0c2-a640-5ea0-b993-a477ec76ed96" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le e,\\,0\\le x\\le \\operatorname{ln}⁡y+1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-8ddecd47-8b29-538f-bf12-0e82ccc9537c" :answer/id #uuid "8ddecd47-8b29-538f-bf12-0e82ccc9537c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le y\\le e,\\,0\\le x\\le {e}^{y+1}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186339051 :question/worked-solution "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type II region has the property that a horizontal line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type II region is the following.\n\n![](images/fe/fe16f5f3d1e9663a7e0df88d71639016bfb3357a6745ee6f125968978fd54c12.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186373174 :question/worked-solution "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nTo express the given region as a type II region, we first rewrite all of the given curves as functions of $y:$\n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,x=\\sqrt{y}\n$$\n\nThe function $x=y$ is already written as a function of $y.$\n\nNotice that the region lies between the horizontal lines $y=0$ and $y=1.$ So, we have $0\\le y\\le 1.$\n\nWe draw a horizontal arrow through the region to determine the left function $g(y)$ and the right function $f(y).$ A horizontal line should intersect the region in a single interval only for it to be a type II region.\n\n![](images/d5/d55cb7ea67d9865368c744577bb4a4b22a3635e8e62869ee65e945612d6c0e98.png)\n\nThe horizontal line enters the region through the lower function $x=y$ and leaves through the upper function $x=\\sqrt{y}.$ So, we have $y\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}.$\n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,y\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}\\}.\n$$" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186373175 :answer-field/correct "answer-a709f16c-6935-5b16-8b38-88908d6454cb" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0747cf82-408b-58c2-b5d7-dcefd0ed68ff" "answer-17567c73-9403-53e0-b46b-a5ceadd85060" "answer-429ef4b8-fbc0-567d-af67-084931824074" "answer-a709f16c-6935-5b16-8b38-88908d6454cb" "answer-4b704cda-a7e0-5c8b-9cf6-66429dfd1ade"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0747cf82-408b-58c2-b5d7-dcefd0ed68ff" :answer/id #uuid "0747cf82-408b-58c2-b5d7-dcefd0ed68ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le 1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-17567c73-9403-53e0-b46b-a5ceadd85060" :answer/id #uuid "17567c73-9403-53e0-b46b-a5ceadd85060" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-429ef4b8-fbc0-567d-af67-084931824074" :answer/id #uuid "429ef4b8-fbc0-567d-af67-084931824074" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le y\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a709f16c-6935-5b16-8b38-88908d6454cb" :answer/id #uuid "a709f16c-6935-5b16-8b38-88908d6454cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,y\\le x\\le \\sqrt{y}\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-4b704cda-a7e0-5c8b-9cf6-66429dfd1ade" :answer/id #uuid "4b704cda-a7e0-5c8b-9cf6-66429dfd1ade" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{2},\\,0\\le x\\le 1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186339049 :question/worked-solution "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type II region has the property that a horizontal line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type II region is the following.\n\n![](images/7c/7c159c025f0b7ae4bfa8984f637a492cda21ec2dd39e87be724324e1334c06a3.png)" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129839 :question/worked-solution "A type II region can be written as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,a\\le y\\le b,\\,g(y)\\le x\\le f(y)\\},\n$$\n\nwhere $f$ and $g$ are continuous functions.\n\nA type II region has the property that a horizontal line drawn through the region intersects the region in a single interval only.\n\nAmong the given options, the only type II region is the following.\n\n![](images/3f/3fccfbd6fd95005958fc9c9c14a1d327c27ef21351b1a32f3a5da553fdbf1539.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186128515 :answer-field/correct 17592186128517 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186403647 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the ellipses $(x-1)^{2}+4{y}^{2}=1$ and ${x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=4?$\n\nI. It is a type I region\n\nII. It is a type II region\n\nIII. It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186284608 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the triangle bounded between the lines $y=1-x,$ $y=x-1,$ and $x=0?$\n\nI. It is a type I region\n\nII. It is a type II region\n\nIII. It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y=1-x\\, & ⟹\\,x=1-y \\\\ y=x-1\\, & ⟹\\,x=y+1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/27/27503f983e3e02fa748bb8ef32966a6cd3b5fff29082ffaf3c10d0521b630e93.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,x-1\\le y\\le 1-x\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- Any horizontal line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le 1-|y|\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type II region.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186401586 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the circle ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=4$ and the ellipse $4{x}^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=1?$\n\nI. It is a type I region\n\nII. It is a type II region\n\nIII. It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186339070 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the parabola $y=4-{x}^{2}$ and the line $y=2-|x|?$\n\nI. It is a type I region\n\nII. It is a type II region\n\nIII. It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/6f/6f35161e7efbd53c9ef558ffe88d8e046771128965a9fdd02143ae37a9b130ea.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,2-|x|\\le y\\le 4-{x}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- The horizontal line $y=1$ intersects the region in two separate intervals, as shown below. So, this can't be a type II region.\n\n![](images/76/769a521cd6b05ecf05052da382e40295b26be66fe56e4eff7c6940c9032f2f0b.png)\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129841 :question/problem "Which of the following statements are true regarding the finite region bounded between the parabola $y=1-{x}^{2}$ and the line $y=-3?$\n\nI. It is a type I region\n\nII. It is a type II region\n\nIII. It's neither a type I nor a type II region" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that\n\n$$\ny=1-{x}^{2}\\,⟹\\,x=\\pm \\sqrt{1-y}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's sketch our region.\n\n![](images/72/726ad8599b89029d3dba8e79ca947af99c17bd8712e551e49fc33d3e597a5cb7.png)\n\nWe have the following:\n\n- Any vertical line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-2\\le x\\le 2,\\,-3\\le y\\le 1-{x}^{2}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type I region.\n\n- Any horizontal line through the region intersects it on a single interval. Furthermore, we can represent our region as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,-3\\le y\\le 1,\\,-\\sqrt{1-y}\\le y\\le \\sqrt{1-y}\\}.\n$$\n\nSo, this is a type II region.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id 17592186129327 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}]
